 "notes": "All 6 planned kinds kept (Sake with brewer's alcohol renamed Honjozo, ginjo & daiginjo; Everyday sake -> Futsūshu; Infused rice wine -> Infused sake). Grades, polishing ratio, kimoto/yamahai, namazake/genshu and koshu are types. Old Akashi-Tai junmai models became versions; 'Akashi-Tai sake range' r dropped (brand in register). Dropped old models SAKE HUNDRED Nikou/Shirin (SKU noise; one SAKE HUNDRED kept). Tozai Typhoon given maker 'Tozai' from its name. Left out: Sho Chiku Bai Classic Junmai, Kubota Manju grade/year, Hakutsuru Awayuki details, Kikusui Funaguchi - sources blocked (masterofmalt/tippsy 429, gltjp/takarasake 403, JETRO 503) or not retrieved. Asahi-Shuzo (Niigata) brand entry from knowledge. Prefecture given in archetype details."
